course: dictionary
lesson: 6310
title: Mortar: one word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. «Places such as a grandparent's house hold memories, so losing them can feel like another loss; "bricks and mortar" means just a building.» Bricks and mortar is about buildings, so mortar must be the stuff that holds the bricks together.
explain: «Then she found an old recipe in Grandma's handwriting, and cooking it with Mum every Sunday made her feel close to Grandma again: places hold memories, but memories live in people, not only in bricks and mortar.» Cooking is not building, but the phrase still means a building here, so the phrase keeps its meaning even in a sentence about recipes.
explain: Ask yourself what the topic is. A builder, a cook, a soldier and a graduation all use mortar in different ways. Read the words around it, try each meaning in the sentence, and keep the one that fits.
fact: Mortar is a mixture of sand, cement or lime and water that sticks bricks or stones together.
fact: A mortar is a strong bowl in which you crush things with a pestle.
fact: A mortar is also a short gun that fires shells high into the air, used in war.
fact: A mortarboard is a flat, square hat worn at graduations.
fact: «Bricks and mortar» means just a building.
exercise: «The builder mixed mortar with sand and water to fix the loose bricks.» What is mortar in this sentence? | A strong bowl for crushing herbs | A flat square hat | A kind of cake | *A mixture used to stick bricks together
exercise: «Dad crushed the peppercorns in a mortar with a pestle.» What is a mortar here? | *A strong bowl for crushing things | A short gun that fires shells | A flat square hat worn at graduations
exercise: «At the graduation, the students tossed their mortarboards into the air.» What is a mortarboard? | A short gun used in war | A strong bowl for crushing things | *A flat, square hat
test: «The soldiers fired a mortar over the hill.» What does mortar mean here? | A bowl for crushing seeds | *A short gun that fires shells high into the air | A mixture of sand and water for bricks
test: «Grandma's house was only bricks and mortar to the estate agent, but to us it was home.» What does bricks and mortar mean here? | A special kind of garden wall | A pile of old bricks ready to sell | A recipe for cooking | *Just a building
exam: «The mason spread fresh mortar between the stones before the wall dried.» What does mortar mean in this sentence? | *A mixture that sticks stones together | A bowl for grinding spices | A flat square hat | A gun that fires shells
